tps://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":656,"digest":"sha256:10553d555ba2b5d677489671a9561907b216116fa871d3bf37c9012864fc479d","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T20:04:10Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T20:04:10Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m1312-v0.13.12/m13stage12-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m1312-v0.13.12","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m1312-v0.13.12","body":"# Engacer OS M13.12 / 0.13.12\n\n**Testing release - whole-product integration qualified, stability pending.** M13.12 passes M13-STAGE12-VM-v1. Historical M13.7/M13.8 freeze reports remain open for M13.13; do not use this testing media for everyday work.\n\n## Download and install\n\nThe release provides the exact ISO, new blank-disk VMware starter, build/starter manifests, native binaries/maps, notices and source/license assets: twenty files with complete SHA-256 checksums. The starter has a new growable 20-GiB SATA disk, two CPUs, 128 MiB RAM, UEFI and Secure Boot off; it is not preinstalled. Extract the entire ZIP and follow the [eight-step installation guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a1f1ad47620cce7e3398be1def1723867bd3d20e/docs/handbook/install-m1312.md) and [first-day guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a1f1ad47620cce7e3398be1def1723867bd3d20e/docs/handbook/final-m1312.md).\n\nBuild: `fb63c329a93bb9e33eef13e05b6723d2`. ISO SHA-256: `1ea953fb49bb4e73a0468eaeda7f5005deeab0f07f9f89db071b1f2613b0c688`. VMware ZIP SHA-256: `507393f979a517f3e9dcc60d221544ddf1ad8ffc90468d5740a9f030fe8c8d88`.\n\n## Final integration\n\nOne frozen build passes **162 native checks, 47 VMware checks, fourteen controller/firmware/starter profiles, 106 independently verified original MSI payloads and 95 app frames**, bound to 613 compiled inputs. Real installation, retained-ISO startup and two independent no-ISO starts pass with all shipped devices enabled and no forced firmware boot order. The exact archived starter passes the supported original 7-Zip MSI install/run/archive/extract/remove/reinstall lifecycle, real protected-worker input service and independently verified data.\n\nWhole-product tasks cover disk tools/consent/protected data/recovery and refusals; desktop selection/shortcuts/overflow/window movement; Start/search/pins; grouped taskbar/tray/USB replacement; Files/history/filter/USB/transfers; owner-bound open/save/extraction dialogs; Settings/search/preview/apply/cancel/preferences; optional-app independence, accessibility and screensaver feature behavior. Actual VMware Preview/wake is independently visible. Five shared display/personalization profiles include compact, ordinary, 150% and real 3840x2160. Nineteen app frames cover three themes at ordinary size and Light at 1024/4K, not every app/theme/scale combination.\n\nThe installed offline guide now explains the current save/cancel controls and screensaver. Measured title/clock alignment and the Appearance search detail finish the existing design without another feature or redesign. [Implementation and decisions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a1f1ad47620cce7e3398be1def1723867bd3d20e/docs/milestones/m13-12.md), [exact acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a1f1ad47620cce7e3398be1def1723867bd3d20e/evidence/M13/12/acceptance-results.json), [resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a1f1ad47620cce7e3398be1def1723867bd3d20e/evidence/M13/12/resources.json), [representative visual review](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a1f1ad47620cce7e3398be1def1723867bd3d20e/evidence/M13/12/visual-review.json).\n\n## Resources and limits\n\nFixed desktop state remains 557,516 bytes (+0 from M13.11), installer state 48,412 bytes and font masks 251,248 bytes. Measured completed tasks retain zero managed pages; configured guest RAM, code, fixed state, framebuffers/shadow and managed peak/retained pages are separate. Independent stopped-image malformed-record cases make no within-session retention claim. No extra worker, framebuffer, cache or idle polling loop is added.\n\nThis is named virtual scope, not universal hardware, physical/ARM support, vendor GPU 3D, arbitrary MSI or general DOS/Windows compatibility. Original Windows support remains the pinned 7-Zip console profile. Screensaver is Off by default, consumes wake gestures and retains the workspace; it provides neither authentication nor display power management. Its one-minute timeout test is a feature check, not stability qualification. Automated scenarios and agent visual review are not a human novice study.\n\n**M13.13 exclusively owns natural-freeze investigation, reset-chain diagnosis and the blocking eight-real-hour stability gate.** This release completes final product integration; it does not claim a freeze fix. Matching actual website delivery is recorded separately after release publication.\n\nOriginal project code remains MIT licensed. Included third-party components retain their own notices, licenses and corresponding source assets.\n"}